  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship)\n(section) § 24.2-404 A 4 (as amended by Chapter 1120; struck words removed, new words kept)\n(quote) 4. Require the general registrars to delete from the record of registered voters the name of any voter who (i) is deceased, (ii) is no longer qualified to vote in the county or city where he is registered due to removal of his residence, (iii) has been convicted of a felony, (iv) has been adjudicated incapacitated, (v) is known not to be a United States citizen by reason of reports from the Department of Motor Vehicles pursuant to § 24.2-410.1 or from the Department of Elections based on information received from the Systematic Alien Verification for Entitlements Program (SAVE Program) pursuant to subsection E, or (vi) is otherwise no longer qualified to vote as may be provided by law.\n(section) § 24.2-404 E (as amended by Chapter 1120; struck words removed, new words kept)\n(quote) E. The Department shall apply to participate in the Systematic Alien Verification for Entitlements Program (SAVE Program) operated by U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services of the U.S. Department of Homeland Security for the sole purpose of individually verifying the current citizenship status of persons who provided documents pursuant to subsection E of § 46.2-328.1. Upon approval of the application, the Department shall enter into any required memorandum of agreement with U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. The State Board shall promulgate rules and regulations governing the use of the immigration status and citizenship status information received from the SAVE Program. The Department shall not (i) use information received from the SAVE Program as the sole reason for rejecting a registration application, (ii) upload lists of registered voters to the SAVE Program for verifying citizenship status in bulk, or (iii) transfer any information to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security or any subdivision thereof beyond the minimum information necessary to use the SAVE Program for the purpose permitted by this subsection.\n(section) § 24.2-427 B (as amended; struck words removed, new words kept)\n(quote) B. Upon receipt of a report from the Department of Motor Vehicles pursuant to § 24.2-410.1 or from the Department of Elections based on information received from the Systematic Alien Verification for Entitlements Program (SAVE Program) pursuant to subsection E of § 24.2-404, the general registrar shall mail notice promptly to all persons listed in the report as not being a citizen of the United States prior to cancelling the registrations of such persons. The notice shall inform the person of the report from the Department of Motor Vehicles or from the Department of Elections and allow the person to submit his sworn statement that he is a United States citizen within 14 days of the date that the notice was mailed. The general registrar shall cancel the registrations of such persons who do not respond within 14 days to the notice that they have been reported not to be United States citizens.\n(other) § 2.2-3711 (two versions): closed meetings authorized for certain limited purposes (existing text reprinted with a conforming change)\n(other) § 24.2-401: persons moving from precinct\n(other) § 24.2-404: duties of Department of Elections (SAVE Program limits in subsection E; list-maintenance duties)\n(other) § 24.2-407.2 (new): security of the Virginia voter registration system\n(other) § 24.2-407.3 (new): list maintenance activities; annual review; report; record matches with confidence score\n(other) § 24.2-408, 409, 410: lists of deceased voters, persons convicted of felonies, certain adjudications\n(other) § 24.2-410.1: lists of noncitizens from Department of Motor Vehicles (identification information fields added)\n(other) § 24.2-410.3 to 410.6 (new): exchange of voter lists with other states; periodic review of registration records; inactive status; return to active status\n(other) § 24.2-426.1 (new): cancellation of registration by voter\n(other) § 24.2-427: cancellation of registration; § 24.2-435: records retention; § 24.2-444: public inspection\n(other) § 24.2-610, 611: materials at polling places; pollbooks\n(other) § 24.2-703.1: permanent absentee voter list (conforming change); § 24.2-709: ballot to be returned in manner prescribed by law (conforming change)\n(other) Sections 24.2-404.3, 404.4, 410.2, 428, 428.1, 428.2 repealed\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
